# Service configuration — shared by bonsai.sh and bonsai-service.sh.
#
# Copy to `bonsai.env` (git-ignored) and edit. Both the interactive
# `./bonsai.sh` commands and the launchd service read it, so they always agree
# on which address and port to use. Anything set in the environment wins over
# this file.
#
#   cp bonsai.env.example bonsai.env
#
# There is no authentication on the server or the bridge. The bind address is
# the access control: leave it on loopback unless you understand what you are
# exposing.

# Bind address for the API server and the Ollama bridge. Defaults to 127.0.0.1.
# To serve your own devices over a VPN (e.g. Tailscale), set the VPN address:
#   BONSAI_HOST="$(tailscale ip -4)"
BONSAI_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Ports.
PORT=8080
BRIDGE_PORT=11434

# Context window for the service. 8192-262144. Leave unset to use the value in
# .bonsai-ctx (which the chat page's context slider writes), else 65536.
# BONSAI_CTX=65536

# Model repo served, OWNER/REPO[:VARIANT]. The default is Bonsai 2 27B at the
# PQ2_0 band; Splash fetches it (plus its DFlash2 draft and vision projector)
# into its own cache on first run.
# BONSAI_SPLASH_MODEL=prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf:PQ2_0

# Free model memory after this much idle time: off (stay loaded), or a Splash
# duration such as 30s / 10m. On a 24 GB machine `10m` returns ~11 GB while
# idle, at the cost of a few seconds on the next request after a long pause.
# BONSAI_IDLE_RELEASE=off